e":"","type":"Near Miss","description":"On February 16, 2026, at approximately 8:30 PM, alternate crew hauler Walter Ayala contacted HSE with a near miss report on Patterson 557. Ayala was running 9 7/8 clincher Tongs #9204  on 7-5/8\" casing, backing out a joint in low gear when the tong hanging line snapped and fell to the rig floor. The tongs remained on the joint on bite and did not fall. All personnel were clear and no one was struck or injured.\n\nAt approximately 9:00 PM, Ayala contacted HSE a second time to report a second hoist line failure on the same rig. The crew had repositioned the tongs to the second hoist line and Ayala was making up a joint in high gear when that line snapped and fell to the rig floor. The tongs remained on the joint on bite and did not fall. No Butch's employees were struck or injured.\n\nBoth hoist lines failed at the same location approximately 60 feet above the rig floor and 56 feet above the tong hanger. No injuries resulted from either event. Classification: Near Miss x2.","location":"Patterson 557","service_line":"Casing","company":"Butch's Rat Hole & Anchor Service Inc","report_number":"76535604"}],"assessments":{"total":20,"details":[{"date":"2026-03-06","assessor":"Laredo Dispatch","form_id":229645,"form_name":"CSG - Pre/Post Trip Inspection","division":"Casing","location":"","report_number":"76605195"},{"date":"2026-03-06","assessor":"Laredo Dispatch","form_id":229645,"form_name":"CSG - Pre/Post Trip Inspection","division":"Casing","location":"","report_number":"76605155"},{"date":"2026-03-06","assessor":"Salvador Ramos","form_id":229645,"form_name":"CSG - Pre/Post Trip Inspection","division":"Casing","location":"","report_number":"76602156"},{"date":"2026-03-06","assessor":"Lee Leon","form_id":229645,"form_name":"CSG - Pre/Post Trip Inspection","division":"Casing","location":"","report_number":"76601915"},{"date":"2026-03-06","assessor":"Rigoberto Perez","form_id":229645,"form_name":"CSG - Pre/Post Trip Inspection","divi